/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
//
// String Table
//

STRINGTABLE 
BEGIN
    IDS_TOOLTIP_ICONTYPE    "How the load is shown in the tray: LED (brightness), Bar (Task Manager style), Clean bar, VU meter (segments), Graph (recent history) or Number."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_INVERT      "Show the 100% value minus the counter value, e.g. memory used from a counter that reports memory available."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_COLORS      "Low, mid and high colour. Click to change. Used by all icon types (the LED uses the low colour)."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_THRESHOLDS  "Where the mid and the high colour start, in % of the scale (the 100% value, or the peak with the Peak and Decay scale)."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_AUTOSTART   "Start this copy of DiskLED when you log on to Windows. Adds a Startup entry for the current user, no admin rights needed."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_VALUEFORMAT "How to show the current value in the icon's tooltip. Use Bytes/s or Bits/s for counters measured in bytes per second, MBytes for counters measured in megabytes."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_UPDATE_FREQUENCY 
                            "How often to update the display (in milliseconds)"
    IDS_TOOLTIP_SCALEMODE   "What corresponds to the full icon. Fixed: the 100% value. Peak: the highest of the last 16 values. Decay: a peak that slowly falls (halves in 30 s). With Peak and Decay the 100% value is the minimum."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_COUNTERSEL  "Which counter the settings below belong to. With a second counter, each counter has its own data source, 100% value, format, scale and warning."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_COUNTER2    "Show a second counter in the same icon: side by side for the bar types, one above the other for graph and number."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_ALERT       "Show a notification when the value stays above this percentage of the 100% value for this many seconds. 0% turns the warning off."
    IDS_TOOLTIP_UPDATE_INI  "Update the INI configuration file when applying settings?"
    IDS_TOOLTIP_DEFAULT_VALUES "Restore default values?"
    IDS_TOOLTIP_100PERCENT  "Which performance counter value corresponds to 100% utilization?"
    IDS_TOOLTIP_COUNTERPATH "From the selection above, build a performance counter path"
    IDS_TOOLTIP_DESCRIPTION "Description of the selected counter"
    IDS_TOOLTIP_OBJECTS     "Select a performance object"
    IDS_TOOLTIP_COUNTERS    "Select a performance object's counter"
    IDS_TOOLTIP_INSTANCES   "Selece a performance counter instance"
END

